re\\'s a message saying \"@mark_johnson is already in here.\" However, he\\'s not showing up in the members list, which suggests he might need to accept the invitation first.\\n\\nSince I cannot see Mark Johnson in the members list to set him as channel leader, and the existing SOP doesn\\'t cover setting users as channel leaders, let me create a new SOP that documents what we\\'ve accomplished and notes the limitation.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'CreatePublicChannelAndInviteUser\\' for platform \\'RocketChat\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'RocketChat', 'operation': 'CreatePublicChannelAndInviteUser', 'details': '# Creating Public Channel and Inviting Users in Rocket.Chat\\n\\n## Steps:\\n1. Navigate to the Rocket.Chat platform homepage\\n2. Click on \"Create Channel\" button from the home screen\\n3. Fill in the channel name (e.g., \"sales-talk\" for #sales-talk channel)\\n4. Ensure the channel is set to public by unchecking the \"Private\" checkbox\\n5. Click on \"Add Members\" field to search for users\\n6. Type the user\\'s name (e.g., \"Mark Johnson\") in the search field\\n7. Select the user from the dropdown list\\n8. Click \"Create\" to create the channel with the selected user\\n\\n## Alternative Method (if user needs to be added after channel creation):\\n1. Open the channel\\n2. Click on \"Members\" button in the toolbar\\n3. Click \"Add\" button in the members panel\\n4. Search for and select the user\\n5. Click \"Add users\" to add them to the channel\\n\\n## Notes:\\n- Users may need to accept invitations before appearing in the members list\\n- The system confirms successful user addition with a message \"The users have been added\"\\n- For setting users as channel leaders, additional role management may be required through channel settings or administration panel\\n- Public channels are visible to all workspace members\\n- **Important**: Users added to channels may not immediately appear in the members list until they accept the invitation or the system processes the addition'}), MCPAction(name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'RocketChat', 'operation': 'SetChannelLeader', 'details': '\\n# Setting Channel Leaders in Rocket.Chat\\n\\n## Current Status: Limited Functionality\\n\\nBased on our exploration of the Rocket.Chat platform, setting users as channel leaders appears to have limitations in the current interface:\\n\\n## Steps Attempted:\\n1. Created public channel #sales-talk successfully\\n2. Invited Mark Johnson to the channel (confirmed with \"The users have been added\" message)\\n3. Attempted to access role management through:\\n   - Channel \"Options\" menu\\n   - \"Room Information\" panel\\n   - \"Edit Room\" settings\\n   - Members list management\\n\\n## Findings:\\n- Users invited to channels may not immediately appear in the members list\\n- Role management options for setting channel leaders were not accessible through the standard UI\\n- The system may require users to accept invitations before they appear in the members list\\n- Channel leader functionality might require administrative privileges or be available through different interface paths\\n\\n## Recommendations:\\n- Wait for invited users to accept invitations before attempting role assignment\\n- Check if administrative access provides additional role management capabilities\\n- Consider using workspace-wide role assignments instead of channel-specific leadership roles\\n- Verify user appears in members list before attempting to assign leadership roles\\n\\n## Current Limitation:\\nUnable to set Mark Johnson as channel leader through the available interface options. The user may need to accept the invitation first, or additional administrative permissions may be required.\\n'}, thought='Now let me also create a specific SOP for setting users as channel leaders, documenting what we learned about the limitations.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'SetChannelLeader\\' for platform \\'RocketChat\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'RocketChat', 'operation': 'SetChannelLeader', 'details': '\\n# Setting Channel Leaders in Rocket.Chat\\n\\n## Current Status: Limited Functionality\\n\\nBased on our exploration of the Rocket.Chat platform, setting users as channel leaders appears to have limitations in the current interface:\\n\\n## Steps Attempted:\\n1. Created public channel #sales-talk successfully\\n2. Invited Mark Johnson to the channel (confirmed with \"The users have been added\" message)\\n3. Attempted to access role management through:\\n   - Channel \"Options\" menu\\n   - \"Room Information\" panel\\n   - \"Edit Room\" settings\\n   - Members list management\\n\\n## Findings:\\n- Users invited to channels may not immediately appear in the members list\\n- Role management options for setting channel leaders were not accessible through the standard UI\\n- The system may require users to accept invitations before they appear in the members list\\n- Channel leader functionality might require administrative privileges or be available through different interface paths\\n\\n## Recommendations:\\n- Wait for invited users to accept invitations before attempting role assignment\\n- Check if administrative access provides additional role management capabilities\\n- Consider using workspace-wide role assignments instead of channel-specific leadership roles\\n- Verify user appears in members list before attempting to assign leadership roles\\n\\n## Current Limitation:\\nUnable to set Mark Johnson as channel leader through the available interface options. The user may need to accept the invitation first, or additional administrative permissions may be required.\\n'}), AgentFinishAction(final_thought='\\nI have successfully completed the task with the following accomplishments:\\n\\n\u2705 **Public #sales-talk channel created**: Successfully created a public channel named \"sales-talk\" in the Rocket.Chat platform.\\n\\n\u2705 **Mark Johnson invited**: Successfully invited Mark Johnson to the channel, with system confirmation \"The users have been added\".\\n\\n\u274c **Channel leader assignment**: Unable to set Mark Johnson as channel leader at this time. The user does not appear in the members list, likely because he needs to accept the invitation first. The Rocket.Chat interface does not provide accessible role management options for setting channel leaders through the standard UI.\\n\\n## Summary of Actions:\\n1. Navigated to the Rocket.Chat platform at http://the-agent-company.com:3000/home\\n2. Created a public channel named \"sales-talk\" \\n3. Unchecked the \"Private\" option to make it public\\n4. Searched for and selected Mark Johnson during channel creation\\n5. Successfully created the channel with Mark Johnson invited\\n6. Attempted multiple approaches to set him as channel leader through various UI elements\\n7. Documented the process and limitations in updated SOPs\\n\\n## Updated SOPs:\\n- Enhanced \"CreatePublicChannelAndInviteUser\" with additional notes about user acceptance delays\\n- Created new \"SetChannelLeader\" SOP documenting the limitations encountered\\n\\nThe channel is now available at http://the-agent-company.com:3000/channel/sales-talk and Mark Johnson has been invited. He will need to accept the invitation before he can be set as channel leader.\\n', task_completed='partial', outputs={}, thought='', action=<ActionType.FINISH: 'finish'>)], inputs={}, outputs={}, agent_state=<AgentState.FINI